agent-service/reports/
agent-service/.playwright-mcp/
# Test-suite snapshots — repo root, not nested under agent-service/, since
# a snapshot bundles content from both agent-service/ and tests/. Two
# exceptions below: OrderFlow's and Uptime Kuma's snapshots are the real
# source of truth tests/support/restore-suite.mjs restores from (CI, the
# hub's demo-switch buttons, and manual Quick Start all use it) — everything
# else in here is still a disposable point-in-time snapshot, gitignored.
# NOTE: `/archive/*` (not `/archive/`) is deliberate — git can't re-include
# a path whose PARENT DIRECTORY itself is excluded (it never descends into
# an excluded dir to check further rules), only a path excluded via a
# wildcard on its contents. See git-scm.com/docs/gitignore's own note on
# this exact limitation.
/archive/*
!/archive/bdd-test-suite-orderflow-2026-08-17T22-03-25-058Z/
!/archive/bdd-test-suite-orderflow-2026-08-17T22-03-25-058Z/**
!/archive/bdd-test-suite-uptime-kuma-2026-08-17T21-56-31-507Z/
!/archive/bdd-test-suite-uptime-kuma-2026-08-17T21-56-31-507Z/**
# Same reasoning as tests/features/tests/steps above, same mechanism —
# loadtests/<descriptor>-load.js (hand-written or AI-generated+approved,
# see agent-service/src/admin/static/load.html) is regenerable/mutable
# content, not something to track directly; a snapshot's own copy (created
# by POST /api/generate/snapshot, restored by tests/support/restore-
# suite.mjs) is the real, git-tracked source of truth instead. The two
# archive/ snapshots allowlisted above function as "the persisted current
# state" (restore-suite.mjs's own restore target), not a literal
# point-in-time historical record — replaced with a fresh round whenever
# the two demo descriptors' own content is untracked/rebased on 2026-08-19.
/loadtests/*.js
# Clones of external target repos (docker-compose component type) — repo
# root, mounted at an identical absolute path on both host and container
# sides; see docker-compose.yml's own comment on this mount for why.
/targets/
# Per-target first-run setup scripts (bootstrap/setupTarget.ts) — same
# targeted-exclusion trick as /archive/* above, same reason: the "Record
# setup" UI (docker-compose.yml's own comment on this directory's mount)
# writes new ones straight to disk, and most of those are exploratory/
# per-user, not meant to land in git automatically. Only artifacts of
# targets in the hub page's own demo block belong in git — uptime-kuma is
# one, nocodb is the record-and-convert workflow's own worked example kept
# alongside it. Trilium (the OTHER record-and-convert validation target)
# was untracked on the same basis 2026-08-14 — still a real local test
# fixture, just not something that belongs in git.
/agent-service/src/bootstrap/setup/*
!/agent-service/src/bootstrap/setup/uptime-kuma.ts
!/agent-service/src/bootstrap/setup/nocodb.ts
# Descriptors themselves (descriptors/<name>.json/.corrections.json/.uat.md/
# .env) — unlike the two exceptions above, NO per-file allowlist here: every
# descriptor is gitignored, including orderflow/uptime-kuma. Their own
# archive/ snapshot (allowlisted above) is now the real source of truth for
# them too — tests/support/restore-suite.mjs restores descriptor.json/
# corrections.json/uat.md/env-overrides.env from it (restore-if-missing,
# never overwrites a live edit), the same script that already restores
# tests/features/tests/steps. The other descriptors here (wger/snipe-it/
# wekan/nopcommerce/kafka-demo/kafka-consumer-demo/nocodb/trilium) have no
# snapshot and no restore path at all — simply gone on a fresh clone, by
# design, same basis Trilium's own files were untracked on 2026-08-14:
# local dev/test fixtures, nothing depends on them being present.
/agent-service/descriptors/*
